                <pb facs="0297" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9873: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tunis</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Heisler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tunis</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-10T19:00:00+02:00">April 10, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 11—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Reliably informed that three Italian destroyers have taken refuge at Sousse;
                    that Tunisia is furnishing the Italian forces in Libya with ammunition and
                    supplies and that Italian vessels are proceeding to Tripoli through Tunisian
                    territorial waters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Heisler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
